<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's Transgas sees sales growth.</title>
<headline>Portugal's Transgas sees sales growth.</headline>
<dateline>OPORTO, Portugal 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese gas distribution company Transgas has signed contracts for sales worth six billion escudos this year and expects to boost sales to 27 billion next year, its president Elias da Costa said.</p>
<p>&quot;In its first year of marketing, Transgas has guaranteed sales of six billion escudos (in 1997), having signed contracts with 41 industrial firms,&quot; he told Reuters.</p>
<p>Costa forecast that sales would rise to between 80 and 100 billion escudos in the year 2000.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
